  |title Task-haste is net-negative, not merely unuseful

  |quote
    task-haste is not just unuseful -- it's net-negative. Thoughtfulness that helps really adjudicate things here thoughtfully is going to be worh so much more than any amount of "output" that's quantitative, however 'coherent' in miniature.

  |occasion
    Closing the night session, before handing over to the morning's work.

  |about
    Quantity of coherent output is not the unit. Hasty work here has to be undone,
    and the undoing costs more than the care would have.

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You are estimating how much you can get through.
    - You are about to produce something rather than adjudicate something.

  |see
    (none recorded yet)
